 "E5": {
  "question": "Can the server hand out a new refresh token when the client refreshes, and what happens to the old one?",
  "answer1": "The server can hand out a new refresh token when the client refreshes, and the old refresh token is typically invalidated but retained by the authorization server. This practice helps in detecting potential refresh token abuse, as described in Section 10.4.",
  "answer2": "Yes, the server can hand out a new refresh token when the client refreshes. In this case, the client must discard the old refresh token and replace it with the new one. The server MAY revoke the old refresh token after issuing a new one. (Section 6)",
